      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">آئِبَةٌ</span></b>  The <i>coming</i> of camels <i>to water, to drink,
every night:</i> whence the saying,
“<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">لَا تَرِدَنَّ المَآءَ إِلَّا آئِبَهْ</span><br />
”
[<i>Do not thou come to the water, to drink, unless
coming to it every night</i>]. (IAar, M.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  See
also <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَيْبَةٌ</span>.

